From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: port Lenovo Tab P12 Pro (q706f) support to v7.3.4

Based on the q706f mainline work by silime (chalkin): https://github.com/silime/linux
(7.1.0-dev). Most of the code in this patch is theirs; file-level copyright and MODULE_AUTHOR lines are kept as found.

q706f-on-7.3.patch (written against silime 7.3.0-dev) re-applied on v7.3.4.
Manual resolutions: dw9768 binding context, hid-multitouch quirk bit
(MT_QUIRK_NO_MODE_REPORTS moves to BIT(27), BIT(26) is taken upstream),
INPUT_QCOM_SPMI_HAPTICS Kconfig placement (silime's hv-haptics entry is not
carried).

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
index ff8a35df78..210823357f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/qcom.yaml
@@ -1108,6 +1108,7 @@ properties:
               - sony,pdx203-generic
               - sony,pdx206-generic
               - xiaomi,elish
+              - xiaomi,enuma
               - xiaomi,pipa
           - const: qcom,sm8250
 
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9768.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9768.yaml
index a0855d3b75..11eb5088e7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9768.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/i2c/dongwoon,dw9768.yaml
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
